# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Austin Rodriguez et al. (2026). Projected Hessian learning: fast curvature supervision for accurate machine-learning interatomic potentials.
#   Machine Learning Science and Technology. doi:10.1088/2632-2153/aeac9b  arXiv:2603.04523v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2603.04523v1 (sha256 34482d4a1acd1f23...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 516 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/rodriguez2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: ANI ensembles (5 seeds) trained on the OpenREACT
# CHON reactant/transition-state/product set (wB97XD/6-31G(d) energies,
# forces and analytic Hessians) with four supervision schemes (E-F,
# E-F-HVP one-column, E-F-HVP PHL, E-F-H). Energy, force and Hessian
# RMSEs on the test, IRC and NMS sets are figure-only (Fig. 3) and only
# relative changes are stated in the text.

